# PoCol Studio, IDE & Viewer: the release manifest public key (SITES-PLAN W14, Q7). OWNER INPUT.
#
# Chrome derives the extension id from the manifest "key" (sha256 of this DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo), so every release
# built with it has one fixed id: users compare it with the id published on pocol.net, and Chrome keeps the extension's
# storage (the studio:wallet vault) across releases loaded from any folder.
#
# The owner replaces the PLACEHOLDER line below with the base64 DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo of the release key, on one
# line (the public half only; the private key never enters this repository). For a Chrome RSA key:
#   openssl rsa -in KEY.pem -pubout -outform DER | base64 -w0
# Then `python3 scripts/package-release.py --extension-id` prints the id to publish.
#
# While the line is the placeholder:
#   - node build.mjs builds dist/ without a manifest "key" (a development build; Chrome gives it an id of its folder);
#   - scripts/package-release.py refuses to package a release.
# Fault, testGateway and rehearsal builds never carry the key, so loading one never replaces a release install.
PLACEHOLDER: the owner's manifest public key (base64 DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo)
